t doesn't exist. It phases in before its controller untaps during their next untap step.)","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"1996-10-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":["W"],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Snow-Covered Plains","oracle_id":"ac8cc74d-e43b-4118-bba0-dfa8b9c04d45","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {W}.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["W"],"released_at":"2021-02-05","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Snow Land — Plains"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"In a Limited event (usually Booster Draft or Sealed Deck), you can't add basic snow lands to your card pool as you would other basic lands. You can play with basic snow lands only if you open them in your sealed deck or draft them.","oracle_id":"ac8cc74d-e43b-4118-bba0-dfa8b9c04d45","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Snow is a supertype, not a card type. It has no rules meaning or function by itself, but spells and abilities may refer to it.","oracle_id":"ac8cc74d-e43b-4118-bba0-dfa8b9c04d45","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Snow isn't a type of mana. If an effect says you may spend mana as though it were any type, you can't pay for {S} using mana that wasn't produced by a snow source.","oracle_id":"ac8cc74d-e43b-4118-bba0-dfa8b9c04d45","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some cards have additional effects for each {S} spent to cast them. You can cast these spells even if you don't spend any snow mana to cast them; their additional effects simply won't do anything.","oracle_id":"ac8cc74d-e43b-4118-bba0-dfa8b9c04d45","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The Kaldheim set doesn't have any cards with mana costs that include {S}, but some previous sets do. If an effect says such a spell costs {1} less to cast, that reduction doesn't apply to any {S} costs. This is also true for activated abilities that include {S} in their activation costs and effects that reduce those costs.","oracle_id":"ac8cc74d-e43b-4118-bba0-dfa8b9c04d45","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The {S} symbol is a generic mana symbol. It represents a cost that can be paid by one mana that was produced by a snow source. That mana can be any color or colorless.","oracle_id":"ac8cc74d-e43b-4118-bba0-dfa8b9c04d45","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The last ability triggers only if that opponent controls more lands than you after the land enters the battlefield. The ability will check again as it tries to resolve. If that opponent doesn't still control more lands than you at that time, the ability won't resolve.","oracle_id":"ef833546-f755-4ac5-867a-3926984e68a0","published_at":"2021-04-16","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
